                         THE STRATFALC EXEs, BATs, AND COMs

           With the release of version 1.2, you've got a rather large
           quantity of executable-type programs in your STRAT directory.
           Here's what they all are and what they all do, in one handy
           section:

                               -Restoration Programs-

           RESTRCAM.BAT
           RESTRCAM is used if for some reason a campaign gets screwed up.
           If you run it *as soon as you realize a campaign is corrupted*,
           it will restore your campaign to the state it was in
           immediately before you last ran StratFalc.  The trick is to
           know when you're campaign is corrupted!  For all intents and
           purposes, it's any time Falcon hangs in the campaign world
           *EXCEPT* for the cases listed below for CLEAR.BAT.

           Each time StratFalc is run, it makes sure a RESTRCAM.BAT
           is available in both the target Falcon directory and the STRAT
           directory.  If it doesn't find one in either place, it puts one
           there, customized for your setup.

           CLEAR.BAT
           CLEAR is used in two specific circumstances.

           First, if Falcon ever hangs *just before you get into the
           cockpit* (meaning:  you zoom down into the cockpit from above,
           but the thing freezes at the top of the aircraft), then you
           should run CLEAR.  This particular freeze up is a symptom of
           NOT having had the STRTSPRT TSR installed during a previous
           mission, so the SQUAD?.MIS file is stilled marked "read-only"





           Strategic FALCON        Version 1.2 Update          Page 12
           ------------------------------------------------------------

           or "hidden."  (The TSR's job is to clear the read-only/hidden
           bit when you end the previous mission.) CLEAR simply clears
           these attributes.

           The second condition under which you should use CLEAR is any
           time you abandon a campaign for any reason.  If you change
           theaters, disband a squadron, etc., before a campaign has
           reached its normal conclusion, run CLEAR to make sure Falcon
           can write all its files normally.

           Like RESTRCAM above, each time StratFalc is run, it makes sure
           a CLEAR.BAT is available in both the target Falcon directory
           and the STRAT directory.  If it doesn't find one in either
           place, it puts one there, customized for your setup.

           ILSRESET.EXE
           In the course of StratFalc events, you move your home base
           around quite a bit.  As detailed in the StratFalc manual,
           modifications are made to the ILS files (ILS.BOS, ILS.IRQ,
           etc.).  ILSRESET puts these files back to their pristine state.
           You really should never have to use it. The only time you'd
           need it is if you start a new campaign and your F-16 does not
           start out on a runway as it's supposed to.

           UNHACK.EXE
           This file is new for version 1.2.  It removes the "Weapons
           Load" hack from Falcon3.exe/Falconcd.exe, just in case you want
           to force the issue.  StratFalc normally keeps these files
           updated as required.

                              -Communications Programs-
            (all these files are new in version 1.2, and their proper use
                      is explained in the COMMs section below)

           305FIX.EXE
           This is a small hack file for Falcon 3.05 only.  It fixes the
           "CANNOT CREATE FILE-SQUAD6.MTV" bug in Falcon.  See 305FIX.DOC
           for information.

           COMMHACK.EXE
           This is another communications-support hack file; it's for both
           Falcon 3.04 and 3.05 only.  It alters Falcon by bypassing the
           normal error routines when the program tries to create and
           write to SQUAD6.MIS.  This allows StratFalc to

           alter the tactical aspects of an allied comms mission and have
           those changes stick.

           It has two modes:  COMMHACK ALTER changes Falcon to allow comms
           support;  COMMHACK RESTORE puts it back to normal.





           Strategic FALCON        Version 1.2 Update          Page 13
           ------------------------------------------------------------

           COMMS304.BAT
           COMMS305.BAT
           These files support comms by making distribution of the altered
           SQUAD6.MIS file semi-automatic.  The appropriate file is copied
           to USER.BAT, then <F6> is used to exit Falcon.

           FALCOM04.BAT
           FALCOM05.BAT
           These files support the above batch files and facilitate
           distribution of the altered SQUAD6.MIS file.  You don't use
           these files directly; the appropriate one is copied as
           "FALCOM.BAT" to the "Sneakernet" disk.

                                 -Utility Programs-

           STRTSPRT.COM
           Stinger's gem that made it all possible.  This file clears the
           hidden/read-only bit from the SQUAD?.MIS file after you end a
           mission in Falcon, and allows creation of the next mission's
           SQUAD?.MIS.

           LOADTSR.BAT
           LT.EXE
           LOADTSR makes sure STRTSPRT is in memory without removing it.
           (Just typing STRTSPRT if the program is in memory will remove
           it.)

           LT.EXE is the core program that makes LOADTSR work.  Note: you
           should never run this program directly;  it requires LOADTSR's
           experienced hand.

           USER.BAT
           This is a batch file for your use.  It's explained in the
           111_READ.ME.  It runs when you exit StratFalc by pressing <F6>.

